## UNDERSTAND THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN A WHITE PAPER AND A YELLOW PAPER

This is a WHITE PAPER review.

The main document should establish the strategic, commercial and operating logic of Universe.

It must be tangible enough to believe, but it should not become a collection of database schemas, implementation tickets or detailed technical specifications.

Use technical detail to establish credibility where necessary. Move extensive engineering detail into an appendix or identify it as material for the Yellow Paper and delivery roadmap.

The white paper should answer:

“Why does this deserve to exist, what will it change, why will people use it, and what is the sensible way to build it?”

The Yellow Paper can answer:

“How exactly will the system, calculations, interfaces and technical controls work?”

Do not confuse these purposes.

Equally, do not allow the white paper to escape difficult practical questions merely because it is a strategic document.

A strategic claim still needs a credible mechanism.


