## THE CENTRAL TEST

For every important idea, ask:

“What does this mean in practice?”

Then:

“Who benefits?”

“What information or capability makes it possible?”

“What does the person actually see or receive?”

“What decision becomes easier or better?”

“What action follows?”

“How will we know whether it worked?”

Finally:

“Would someone keep using this when the novelty and any incentive disappear?”

An idea that cannot answer these questions needs clarification, redesign, deferral or removal.


